private/

# Harness output. `tests/parktables.check.js --shots` writes screenshots here so a
# visual change can be LOOKED at rather than asserted about; they are evidence for one
# session, not artifacts of the site. The temp render + compiled stylesheet the same
# harness writes are deleted on exit, and listed here for the run that crashes first.
tests/__shots/
games/park-tables/__pt_test.html
assets/css/__pt_test.css

# `npm run sim:bots` writes its ladder measurement here (2026-09-12). It is a READING —
# what the bots scored on one seed, on one machine, on one afternoon — not a fact about
# the site, and a committed one would go stale silently and then be quoted as current.
# The seed is printed at the top of every run, so any result can be reproduced instead.
#   ⚠ NAMED TWO FILES FIRST AND THAT WAS THE WRONG RULE — one afternoon of sharded runs
#   left TWELVE untracked result files (price-1..4, weak-1..2, shard-dry-1..4, dry-weak,
#   sim-seed7). A results file is disposable by nature, so the rule has to be a pattern.
tests/sim-bots.out.txt
tests/sim-smoke.txt
tests/sim-seed*.txt
tests/price-*.txt
tests/weak-*.txt
tests/shard-dry-*.txt
tests/dry-weak.txt
tests/rr-*.txt
tests/fit-*.txt
tests/map-*.txt
#   ⚠ THIRD TIME A RULE HERE WAS WRITTEN TOO NARROW (2026-09-13). First two named files
#   when twelve existed; then the patterns missed `map-final.txt`. Any NEW sim output
#   belongs in this block the moment the mode that writes it is added, not afterwards.
